# QuasarEdu — Cursor AI Rules
# Scholarship Management System
# Project QuasarX

## Project Purpose
Full-stack web application for end-to-end scholarship management for educational institutions.

## Tech Stack
- Frontend: React 18, React Router v6, Tailwind CSS
- Backend: Node.js 20 LTS, Express.js
- Database: MySQL 8 — raw SQL queries only, no ORM
- AI/OCR: Google Gemini 2.5 Flash API (document auto-fill + chatbot)
- PDF: Puppeteer (application receipts with QR code)
- QR: qrcode npm package
- Auth: JWT (jsonwebtoken) + bcrypt
- Email: Nodemailer with Gmail SMTP
- File uploads: Multer (whitelist: .pdf, .jpg, .jpeg, .png only)

## Project Structure
client/src/pages/         Student and Admin pages
client/src/components/    Reusable UI components
client/src/services/      API call functions (axios)
server/routes/            One file per resource: auth, students, scholarships, applications, admin
server/controllers/       Business logic separated from routes
server/middleware/         auth.js, upload.js, rateLimiter.js
server/db/                MySQL connection pool (mysql2)
database/                 schema.sql, stored-procedures.sql, seed.sql

## Database Entities (10 tables, all in 3NF)
Users, Students, Scholarships, Applications, Documents,
Notifications, SavedScholarships, IdentityVerificationTokens,
FingerprintVerificationTokens, ApplicationDocuments

## Key Business Rules
- A student may apply once per scholarship; re-apply only after Rejected or Withdrawn
- Application submission requires: profile complete (13 fields) + identity verified
- Identity verification = face selfie + fingerprint/biometric/PIN via secure token link
- Eligibility filters: MinimumCGPA, MaxFamilyIncome, DegreeProgram, SemesterYear
- OTP: 6-digit, 5-minute expiry, max 3 attempts
- Brute-force: 15-minute lockout after 5 failed login attempts (students only)
- Verification tokens: 64-char hex, single-use, 1-hour expiry, atomic claim
- File uploads: whitelist .pdf .jpg .jpeg .png only
- CGPA range: 0.0 – 4.0 (Pakistani grading scale) — empty value must fail validation, not pass silently
- Semester range: 1–8 for BS, 1–4 for MS
- Family income: PKR, positive number only

## Application Status Values
Pending | Approved | Rejected | Withdrawn | Draft

## Roles
Student | Admin

## Coding Conventions
- Use async/await throughout, no callbacks
- All DB queries use parameterized statements (mysql2 ? placeholders) — never string concatenation
- Controllers return consistent JSON: { success: true, data: ... } or { success: false, message: ... }
- HTTP status codes: 200, 201, 400, 401, 403, 404, 500
- JWT stored in httpOnly cookie, not localStorage
- All routes under /api/v1/
- Student routes protected by auth middleware checking role === 'Student'
- Admin routes protected by auth middleware checking role === 'Admin'
- Multer stores files as: email_documentType_timestamp.ext
- Use dotenv for all secrets — never hardcode credentials

## Frontend Conventions
- Tailwind only for styling
- Component names: PascalCase
- File names: kebab-case
- API calls go in /services/ files, not inside components
- React Router v6 for all navigation
- Toast notifications for all success/error feedback
- Color palette: teal (#0E7490) primary, white backgrounds, color-coded status badges
- All forms use react-hook-form + zodResolver — never raw useState for form state, never uncontrolled inputs
- Numeric fields (CGPA, income, semester) must use z.coerce.number() in zod schema — submitted data must be typed correctly, not raw strings
- Every input must have: <label htmlFor> matching input id, aria-describedby linking to error element, aria-invalid, and errors must have role="alert"
- Validation mode: onBlur for field errors, first invalid field gets focus on submit via setFocus()

## Pages to Build
- /login
- /register → /verify-otp
- /forgot-password
- /dashboard (student)
- /profile (tabs: Personal, Academic, Address, Education, Documents)
- /scholarships/:id/apply
- /my-applications
- /notifications
- /admin/dashboard
- /admin/applications/:id/review
- /admin/scholarships/new and /:id/edit
- /admin/students
- Floating chatbot widget on all student pages

## Do Not
- Do not use an ORM — raw mysql2 queries only
- Do not store JWT in localStorage — httpOnly cookies only
- Do not skip parameterized queries on any DB call
- Do not allow file uploads outside the whitelist
- Do not use useState for form field values — use react-hook-form
- Do not add fields, components, or features not explicitly in the spec — scope creep from AI output must be caught in review
- Do not skip tests after generating a form or component — always request Vitest tests in the same prompt